{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01: Grammar-guided node reduction (Perses-style)\n\nThe algorithm:\n1. Consider nodes in order: deeper nodes before shallower ones (descending depth)\n2. At equal depth, use node ID as stable tie-break\n3. Never remove: root, a node whose symbol is in `required_symbols`, or a node with retained children\n4. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented after removal\n5. Track removal order and retained nodes\n\nLet me think through the algorithm:\n\n1. Build a tree structure from the nodes\n2. Process nodes in order: deepest first, ties broken by node ID (lexicographic? or by position in input?)\n3. For each node (in that order), try to remove it:\n   - Skip if not removable\n   - Skip if symbol is required\n   - Skip if it has retained children\n   - Check if removing it would still leave all required symbols represented\n   - If yes, remove it (add to removed list)\n   - If no, keep it (add to retained list)\n4. Return removed_node_ids (in removal order) and retained_node_ids (sorted)\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" - process deepest first.\n\n\"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" - at same depth, sort by node ID.\n\nNode IDs are strings like \"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", etc. Lexicographic ordering: \"n1\" \u003c \"n2\" \u003c \"n3\" etc., \"root\" would come after \"n\" strings lexicographically... wait, 'r' \u003e 'n' so \"root\" \u003e \"n6\". But \"root\" has depth 0 which is the shallowest so it won't tie with others typically.\n\n\"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\n\"Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented.\"\n\nLet me trace through case 000:\n\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root\n- n1: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1\n- n2: depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2\n- n3: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0\n- n4: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols = [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nProcessing order (deepest first, then by node ID):\n- Depth 2: n4, n5, n6\n- Depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n- Depth 0: root\n\nCurrent retained set (all nodes initially): {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n6}\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1):\n- Symbol s1 is required! So we cannot remove it... wait.\n- \"Never remove... a required symbol\" - does this mean a node whose symbol is in required_symbols?\n- Yes, symbol=s1 and s1 is in required_symbols, so cannot remove n4.\n- n4 is retained.\n\nProcess n5 (depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2):\n- Not removable, so skip (retain).\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0):\n- symbol=s0, not in required_symbols\n- No children (it's a leaf), so no retained children issue\n- If we remove n6, remaining retained symbols = {root (root), s1 (n1), s2 (n2), s0 (n3), s1 (n4), s2 (n5)}\n- required_symbols = [root, s1] - both still present\n- Remove n6!\n\nProcess n1 (depth=1, removable=false):\n- Not removable, retain.\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2):\n- symbol=s2, not required\n- Children: n4. n4 is currently retained (not removed). So n2 has retained children → cannot remove.\n- Retain n2.\n\nProcess n3 (depth=1, removable=false):\n- Not removable, retain.\n\nProcess root (depth=0, removable=false):\n- Not removable, retain.\n\nResult:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n6\"] (in removal order)\n- retained_node_ids: sorted [\"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nWait, \"root\" lexicographically... 'r' = 114, 'n' = 110, so \"root\" \u003e \"n*\". So sorted: [\"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\", \"root\"].\n\nLet me now implement solve(case) in Python:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in [\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"]:\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing field {field} in node\")\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {node[\"id\"]: [] for node in nodes}\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[node[\"parent\"]].append(node[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Sort nodes: deeper first, then by node ID (lexicographic) as tie-break\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    # Track which nodes are retained\n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        # Check if removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        # Check if symbol is required\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        # Check if has retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(child in retained for child in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        # Check if all required symbols remain represented if we remove this node\n        # Current retained symbols (excluding this node)\n        remaining_symbols = set()\n        for other_id in retained:\n            if other_id != nid:\n                # find symbol\n                pass\n        # Better: build id-\u003esymbol map\n        # ... let me restructure\n        pass\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nLet me write a cleaner version:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate\n    required_node_fields = {\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"}\n    for node in nodes:\n        missing = required_node_fields - set(node.keys())\n        if missing:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node missing fields: {missing}\")\n    \n    # Build lookup structures\n    id_to_node = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            if node[\"parent\"] not in id_to_node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Parent {node['parent']} not found\")\n            children[node[\"parent\"]].append(node[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Sort: deeper first, then by node ID lexicographically\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    retained = set(n[\"id\"] for n in nodes)\n    removed_order = []\n    \n    # id -\u003e symbol for quick lookup\n    id_to_symbol = {n[\"id\"]: n[\"symbol\"] for n in nodes}\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        # Must be removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        # Symbol must not be required\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        # Must not have retained children\n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        # Check if removing preserves all required symbols\n        # Symbols still present after hypothetical removal\n        remaining_symbols = {id_to_symbol[rid] for rid in retained if rid != nid}\n        if required_symbols.issubset(remaining_symbols):\n            retained.remove(nid)\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": sorted(retained)\n    }\n```\n\nLet me verify with case 000:\n\nNodes sorted (deepest first, then by ID):\n- depth=2: n4, n5, n6\n- depth=1: n1, n2, n3\n- depth=0: root\n\nretained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n6}\n\nProcess n4: symbol=s1, in required_symbols → skip\nProcess n5: removable=false → skip\nProcess n6: removable=true, symbol=s0 (not required), no retained children (n6 has no children)\n  - remaining_symbols = {root, s1, s2, s0, s1, s2} = {root, s1, s2, s0}\n  - required = {root, s1} ⊆ {root, s1, s2, s0} ✓\n  - Remove n6!\n\nretained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\nremoved_order = [\"n6\"]\n\nProcess n1: removable=false → skip\nProcess n2: removable=true, symbol=s2 (not required), children={n4}, n4 in retained → has retained children → skip\nProcess n3: removable=false → skip\nProcess root: removable=false → skip\n\nFinal:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n6\"]\n- retained_node_ids: sorted({\"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\"}) = [\"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nCase 001: Same structure, same symbols, same removable flags. Should get same result.\n\nCase 002: Same structure. Same result.\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me now format it as the required JSON output.\n\nThe output must be:\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}\n```\n\nLet me write the clean Python code and encode it properly.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    required_node_fields = {\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\"}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        missing = required_node_fields - set(node.keys())\\n        if missing:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Node missing required fields: {missing}\\\")\\n\\n    if not nodes:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"nodes list is empty\\\")\\n\\n    # Build lookup structures\\n    id_to_node = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    id_to_symbol = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n[\\\"symbol\\\"] for n in nodes}\\n\\n    # Build children map\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        p = node[\\\"parent\\\"]\\n        if p is not None:\\n            if p not in id_to_node:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Parent id '{p}' not found in node list\\\")\\n            children[p].append(node[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Sort: deeper nodes first; ties broken by node ID lexicographically\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    retained = set(n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes)\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Must be marked removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node whose symbol is required\\n        if node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node that still has retained children\\n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentatively remove: check all required symbols still represented\\n        remaining_symbols = {id_to_symbol[rid] for rid in retained if rid != nid}\\n        if required_symbols.issubset(remaining_symbols):\\n            retained.remove(nid)\\n            removed_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01MfVAH3vfrL0nxo3u7YC83T","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2538,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":52,"output_tokens":3161,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2577},"service_tier":"standard"}}